A||||8||Johnson's85SE||My idle desided to increase||||13||
Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||05-03-2001||12:59 PM||||Hi,<BR> My idle has increased to between 1900 - 1500 Rpm. What could have caused this? Also, The tube that runs into the valve cover to the air intake is making my throttle body dirty. Is this supposed to be a constant cleaning item? <BR>Thanks,<BR> <P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||13
Z||000001||84Bill||05-03-2001||01:03 PM||||Replace the PCV valve and clean everything up If it still crudds up with oil ya got alot of blow by and nothing short of an overhaul will fix it.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-03-2001||02:09 PM||||A vacuum leak is the most likely cause of high idle.  If you have a v-6 then after you look for obvious disconnected/broken vacuum lines look at the EGR tube.  This is the corrugated metal tube covered with an insulating blanket thet runs from the EGR valve to the underside of the red intake plenum.  <P>With the engine running wiggle this tube to see if the rpms change.  You can also spray WD-40 between the insulation and the tube to see if it gets sucked in and makes the rpms change.<P>New tubes are pretty expensive, maybe $100.00 US or so.  Aftermarket ones are more flexible.  The tube for the late 80s model Pontiac 6000 2.8 L engine and maybe the Camaro one also fits with just a bit of modification.  The flange bolt holes of one end need to be slotted.  These tubes are more plentiful at junkyards and don't cost as much new.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||05-06-2001||12:21 PM||||EGR could be dirty inside also,where the valve meets the seat;easy to scrape clean once removed.My four cylinder car required this a couple of times.||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||05-06-2001||03:33 PM||||Yup, vaccuum leak....is it a V6 or 4banger? If its a V6, Id say check the EGR tube first. M7F||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jncomutt||05-06-2001||08:03 PM||||Hey, I have the same problem with my 4banger!  I just replaced distributer cap, rotor, plugs, wires, oil.... It still idles high...<P>What your think I should try for my 4cyl?  Would it be the same things to check as the v6?  Also, could this high idle have the same problem behind it that causes my car to misfire at idle as well???||||reg||1
Z||000006||HummelHund||05-07-2001||05:17 PM||||Jncomutt, go borrow yourself a timing light if you don't have one and use the Haynes, Chilton, or service manual instructions to check and reset the timing on your Fiero. The same thing was happening to my '84 until I adjusted the timing (it was off the scale), it stopped the stumbling and helped my idle to some extent. Also check all your vaccuum hoses and your TBI mounting bolt torque. It could also be your IAC, pull it out and clean it, also push gently on it to see if it's not seized. Don't push too hard, though, as you could break it. <BR>Hope this helps,<P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Johnson's85SE||05-07-2001||05:34 PM||||Hey, You want to know the wierdest thing. Since it has warmed up out here in Calgary. My idle has decreased to 1000 to 1500. And to answer other questions, mine is a V6 4SPD. When I depress my EGR MY car does stall so I dont think there is a EGR Vacuum Leak. What else could it be? <BR>Thanks,<BR><P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JasonS||05-08-2001||08:33 AM||||You know.  I had a high idle problem. It stayed at 2000 rpm.  I just dealt with it until a friend of mine suggested something.  Take a pair of channel locks and work the throttle body bracket that the throttle cable attaches to.  Sometimes the throttle doesn't close enough, thus making the idle high.  Now my idle averages around 750 rpm. Just something quick to try before you spend a lot of time scratching your head.||||reg||3
